# SDT memo skill

A memo is a planned operation the register owns; SDT has no scheduler, so the
due check is opportunistic and propose-never-block.

1. Read `context/instructions/memo.md` **before any register write** — the
   rule/memo model, the CLI-owned register and the due-check contract live
   there.
2. Mutate only through the CLI (`sdt context memo …`), never by hand-editing
   the register.
3. At session start, run `sdt context memo due`; surface what is due and ask
   whether to run it before or after the requested task — never block the task,
   never run it silently.
4. A due operation the user declines is postponed, not dropped: the register
   records it and its next due date.
